{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Kronicle — Interactive Walkthrough\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook walks through setting up and using Kronicle step by step.\n",
        "Each cell can be executed independently (assuming prior cells in the same section have run).\n",
        "\n",
        "**Sections:**\n",
        "1. [Setup & Pull](#1.-Setup-&-Pull)\n",
        "2. [First Run — Default Config](#2.-First-Run-—-Default-Config)\n",
        "3. [First Channel — Write & Read](#3.-First-Channel-—-Write-&-Read)\n",
        "4. [Run With User Config](#4.-Run-With-User-Config)\n",
        "5. [RBAC Setup](#5.-RBAC-Setup)\n",
        "6. [Testing the App (Dev)](#6.-Testing-the-App-(Dev))\n",
        "7. [Appendix](#7.-Appendix)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## 1. Setup & Pull\n",
        "\n",
        "Pull the Kronicle container image and verify it's available."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Pull the latest Kronicle image\n",
        "!podman pull ghcr.io/logistica-dev/kronicle:latest"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Verify the image is available\n",
        "!podman images | grep kronicle"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## 2. First Run — Default Config\n",
        "\n",
        "Start Kronicle with the minimum required configuration.\n",
        "On first boot, the app auto-initialises the database, creates tables, and seeds a superuser."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 2.1 Generate superuser credentials\n",
        "\n",
        "The `KRONICLE_SU_INFO` variable requires a base64url-encoded triplet of `name:email:argon2_hashed_password`.\n",
        "A helper script produces this for you:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Generate the superuser credentials string\n",
        "# Replace the name, email, and password with your own\n",
        "!python3 ./scripts/utils/hash_creds.py KronicleAdmin admin@kronicle.app \"KronicleAdmin_Passw0rd\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Copy the output and use it as `KRONICLE_SU_INFO` in the `.env` file below."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 2.2 Create a minimal `.env` file"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "%%writefile .env\n",
        "# Database superuser (only needed for init + migrations)\n",
        "POSTGRES_USER=postgres\n",
        "POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres\n",
        "\n",
        "# App database name (optional, defaults to kronicle_db)\n",
        "KRONICLE_DB_NAME=kronicle_db\n",
        "\n",
        "# Superuser credentials (output of hash_creds.py)\n",
        "KRONICLE_SU_INFO=S3JvbmljbGVBZG1pbjphZG1pbkBrcm9uaWNsZS5hcHA6JGFyZ29uMmlkJHY9MTkkbT02NTUzNix0PTMscD00JGVkSE56VDc2YjRXUitiMEowTDRObFEkbkZRNVJqclkreG56QkMzbnZma2Z2OEI0N1YvY2lwbGF5Y1VGUUtzS2pZaw\n",
        "\n",
        "# DB users for channel data and RBAC (base64url-encoded user:pass)\n",
        "KRONICLE_CHAN_CREDS=Y2hhbl91c3JfbmFtZTpjaGFuX3Vzcl9wYXNz\n",
        "KRONICLE_RBAC_CREDS=cmJhY191c3JfbmFtZTpyYmFjX3Vzcl9wYXNz\n",
        "\n",
        "# Server config\n",
        "KRONICLE_PORT=8000\n",
        "KRONICLE_HOST=0.0.0.0\n",
        "KRONICLE_ENV=test\n",
        "KRONICLE_LOG_LEVEL=3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 2.3 Start the server"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!podman-compose up -d"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Wait for the server to be ready (check logs)\n",
        "!podman-compose logs -f app &\n",
        "import time\n",
        "time.sleep(5)\n",
        "!podman-compose logs --tail 20 app"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 2.4 Verify health"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import urllib.request\n",
        "import json\n",
        "\n",
        "def http_get(path):\n",
        "    url = f\"http://localhost:8000{path}\"\n",
        "    resp = urllib.request.urlopen(url)\n",
        "    return json.loads(resp.read())\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Liveness: \", http_get(\"/health/live\"))\n",
        "print(\"Readiness:\", http_get(\"/health/ready\"))\n",
        "print(\"Version:  \", http_get(\"/health/version\"))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 2.5 Login and get an access token\n",
        "\n",
        "Open the Swagger UI at [http://localhost:8000/docs](http://localhost:8000/docs), or use the API directly:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import urllib.request\n",
        "import json\n",
        "\n",
        "def api_post(path, body):\n",
        "    url = f\"http://localhost:8000{path}\"\n",
        "    data = json.dumps(body).encode()\n",
        "    req = urllib.request.Request(url, data=data, headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"})\n",
        "    resp = urllib.request.urlopen(req)\n",
        "    return json.loads(resp.read())\n",
        "\n",
        "# Login as superuser\n",
        "login_resp = api_post(\"/auth/v1/login\", {\n",
        "    \"name\": \"KronicleAdmin\",\n",
        "    \"password\": \"KronicleAdmin_Passw0rd\"\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "TOKEN = login_resp[\"access_token\"]\n",
        "print(f\"Token obtained: {TOKEN[:20]}...\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Helper for authenticated requests\n",
        "def api_auth_get(path):\n",
        "    url = f\"http://localhost:8000{path}\"\n",
        "    req = urllib.request.Request(url, headers={\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {TOKEN}\"})\n",
        "    resp = urllib.request.urlopen(req)\n",
        "    return json.loads(resp.read())\n",
        "\n",
        "def api_auth_post(path, body):\n",
        "    url = f\"http://localhost:8000{path}\"\n",
        "    data = json.dumps(body).encode()\n",
        "    req = urllib.request.Request(url, data=data, headers={\n",
        "        \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n",
        "        \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {TOKEN}\"\n",
        "    })\n",
        "    resp = urllib.request.urlopen(req)\n",
        "    return json.loads(resp.read())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## 3. First Channel — Write & Read\n",
        "\n",
        "Create a channel with a schema, insert rows, and query them back."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 3.1 Create a channel with data\n",
        "\n",
        "The `POST /data/v1/channels` endpoint accepts an `InputPayload`:\n",
        "- `channel_schema`: column definitions (`{name: type}`)\n",
        "- `name`: channel name (auto-normalised)\n",
        "- `metadata`: arbitrary key-value metadata\n",
        "- `tags`: key-value tags for filtering\n",
        "- `rows`: list of data points"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from datetime import datetime, timedelta\n",
        "\n",
        "now = datetime.now()\n",
        "\n",
        "channel_payload = {\n",
        "    \"name\": \"room-temperatures\",\n",
        "    \"channel_schema\": {\n",
        "        \"time\": \"datetime\",\n",
        "        \"temperature\": \"float\",\n",
        "        \"humidity\": \"float\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    \"metadata\": {\n",
        "        \"location\": \"building-A\",\n",
        "        \"unit_temp\": \"celsius\",\n",
        "        \"unit_humidity\": \"percent\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    \"tags\": {\n",
        "        \"floor\": \"3\",\n",
        "        \"type\": \"environment\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    \"rows\": [\n",
        "        {\"time\": (now - timedelta(hours=3)).isoformat(), \"temperature\": 21.5, \"humidity\": 55.0},\n",
        "        {\"time\": (now - timedelta(hours=2)).isoformat(), \"temperature\": 22.0, \"humidity\": 54.0},\n",
        "        {\"time\": (now - timedelta(hours=1)).isoformat(), \"temperature\": 22.3, \"humidity\": 53.5},\n",
        "        {\"time\": now.isoformat(), \"temperature\": 22.1, \"humidity\": 54.2},\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "result = api_auth_post(\"/data/v1/channels\", channel_payload)\n",
        "CHANNEL_ID = result[\"id\"]\n",
        "print(f\"Channel created: {result['name']} (id: {CHANNEL_ID})\")\n",
        "print(f\"Schema: {result['channel_schema']}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Rows inserted: {result.get('op_details', {}).get('inserted_row_count', 'N/A')}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 3.2 List channels"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "channels = api_auth_get(\"/api/v1/channels\")\n",
        "for ch in (channels if isinstance(channels, list) else [channels]):\n",
        "    print(f\"  {ch['name']} — {ch.get('row_count', '?')} rows — tags: {ch.get('tags', {})}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 3.3 Read rows"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "rows = api_auth_get(f\"/api/v1/channels/{CHANNEL_ID}/rows\")\n",
        "print(f\"Rows for '{rows['name']}\":\")\n",
        "for row in rows.get(\"rows\", []):\n",
        "    print(f\"  t={row['time']}  temp={row['temperature']}°C  hum={row['humidity']}%\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 3.4 Query with filters\n",
        "\n",
        "Filter rows using query parameters:\n",
        "- `{col}` — exact match\n",
        "- `{col}.min` — minimum value (>=)\n",
        "- `{col}.max` — maximum value (<=)\n",
        "- `{col}.any` — value in list\n",
        "- `{col}.has` — array contains value"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Get rows where temperature >= 22.0\n",
        "filtered = api_auth_get(f\"/api/v1/channels/{CHANNEL_ID}/rows?temperature.min=22.0\")\n",
        "print(\"Rows with temperature >= 22.0:\")\n",
        "for row in filtered.get(\"rows\", []):\n",
        "    print(f\"  t={row['time']}  temp={row['temperature']}°C\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 3.5 Append more rows"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "append_payload = {\n",
        "    \"rows\": [\n",
        "        {\"time\": (now + timedelta(hours=1)).isoformat(), \"temperature\": 21.8, \"humidity\": 55.5},\n",
        "        {\"time\": (now + timedelta(hours=2)).isoformat(), \"temperature\": 21.2, \"humidity\": 56.0},\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "result = api_auth_post(f\"/data/v1/channels/{CHANNEL_ID}/rows\", append_payload)\n",
        "print(f\"Rows inserted: {result.get('op_details', {}).get('inserted_row_count', 'N/A')}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Total rows: {result.get('op_details', {}).get('total_row_count', 'N/A')}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## 4. Run With User Config\n",
        "\n",
        "Override default settings by providing a custom INI file and secrets."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 4.1 Create a custom config file\n",
        "\n",
        "Copy the default config and adjust values:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "%%writefile .conf/my-conf.ini\n",
        "[app]\n",
        "version='1.0.0'\n",
        "name='My Kronicle'\n",
        "\n",
        "[auth]\n",
        "pwd_min_length=8\n",
        "pwd_require_special=false\n",
        "\n",
        "[jwt]\n",
        "expiration_minutes=60\n",
        "algorithm=HS256\n",
        "\n",
        "[rbac]\n",
        "reserved_names=superuser,admin,anonymous\n",
        "allow_anonymous=true\n",
        "\n",
        "[db]\n",
        "; DB credentials are read from environment variables, not here"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 4.2 Create a secrets file"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "%%writefile .conf/.secrets\n",
        "POSTGRES_USER=postgres\n",
        "POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres\n",
        "KRONICLE_DB_NAME=kronicle_db\n",
        "KRONICLE_SU_INFO=S3JvbmljbGVBZG1pbjphZG1pbkBrcm9uaWNsZS5hcHA6JGFyZ29uMmlkJHY9MTkkbT02NTUzNix0PTMscD00JGVkSE56VDc2YjRXUitiMEowTDRObFEkbkZRNVJqclkreG56QkMzbnZma2Z2OEI0N1YvY2lwbGF5Y1VGUUtzS2pZaw\n",
        "KRONICLE_CHAN_CREDS=Y2hhbl91c3JfbmFtZTpjaGFuX3Vzcl9wYXNz\n",
        "KRONICLE_RBAC_CREDS=cmJhY191c3JfbmFtZTpyYmFjX3Vzcl9wYXNz\n",
        "KRONICLE_PORT=8000\n",
        "KRONICLE_HOST=0.0.0.0\n",
        "KRONICLE_ENV=test\n",
        "KRONICLE_LOG_LEVEL=3\n",
        "KRONICLE_CONF=/opt/kronicle/conf/my-conf.ini"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 4.3 Restart with custom config\n",
        "\n",
        "Note: the custom INI file needs to be mounted into the container. For local dev, use `uvicorn` directly:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# For docker: mount the conf directory in docker-compose.yml\n",
        "# For local dev:\n",
        "# KRONICLE_CONF=.conf/my-conf.ini uvicorn kronicle.main:app --reload --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n",
        "\n",
        "# Verify anonymous access is now enabled\n",
        "try:\n",
        "    anon_resp = http_get(\"/api/v1/channels\")\n",
        "    print(\"Anonymous access works:\", anon_resp)\n",
        "except Exception as e:\n",
        "    print(f\"Anonymous access denied (expected if no anonymous policy): {e}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## 5. RBAC Setup\n",
        "\n",
        "This section demonstrates the full RBAC workflow:\n",
        "1. Create zones and channels\n",
        "2. Create users and groups\n",
        "3. Assign roles and create policies\n",
        "4. Verify access control\n",
        "\n",
        "We use the [`kronicle-sdk`](https://pypi.org/project/kronicle-sdk/) for convenience, but everything can be done via the raw API."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 5.1 Install the SDK"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!pip install kronicle-sdk -q"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 5.2 Connect as superuser"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import os\n",
        "\n",
        "os.environ[\"KRONICLE_HOST\"] = \"localhost\"\n",
        "os.environ[\"KRONICLE_PORT\"] = \"8000\"\n",
        "os.environ[\"KRONICLE_SU_NAME\"] = \"KronicleAdmin\"\n",
        "os.environ[\"KRONICLE_SU_PASS\"] = \"KronicleAdmin_Passw0rd\"\n",
        "\n",
        "from kronicle_sdk.conf.read_conf import Settings\n",
        "from kronicle_sdk.connectors.rbac.rbac_setup import KronicleRbac\n",
        "from kronicle_sdk.connectors.rbac.core_setup import KronicleCore\n",
        "from kronicle_sdk import KronicleWriter, KronicleReader\n",
        "\n",
        "co = Settings().connection_su\n",
        "\n",
        "rbac = KronicleRbac.from_connection_info(co)\n",
        "core = KronicleCore.from_connection_info(co)\n",
        "writer = KronicleWriter.from_connection_info(co)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Connected as superuser:\", co.usr)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 5.3 Create zones"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from kronicle_sdk.models.rbac.kronicle_zone import KronicleZone\n",
        "\n",
        "zone_a = core.create_zone(KronicleZone(name=\"lab-sensors\"))\n",
        "zone_b = core.create_zone(KronicleZone(name=\"weather-station\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Zone A: {zone_a.name} (id: {zone_a.id})\")\n",
        "print(f\"Zone B: {zone_b.name} (id: {zone_b.id})\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 5.4 Create channels in zones"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from kronicle_sdk.models.data.kronicle_channel import KronicleChannel\n",
        "from kronicle_sdk.models.iso_datetime import now_local\n",
        "\n",
        "schema = {\"time\": \"datetime\", \"value\": \"float\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "chan1 = writer.create_channel(\n",
        "    KronicleChannel(\n",
        "        name=\"lab-temp-1\",\n",
        "        channel_schema=schema,\n",
        "        tags={\"zone\": \"lab\"},\n",
        "        rows=[\n",
        "            {\"time\": now_local(), \"value\": 21.5},\n",
        "            {\"time\": now_local(), \"value\": 22.0},\n",
        "        ],\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "    zone_id=zone_a.id,\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "chan2 = writer.create_channel(\n",
        "    KronicleChannel(\n",
        "        name=\"lab-temp-2\",\n",
        "        channel_schema=schema,\n",
        "        tags={\"zone\": \"lab\"},\n",
        "        rows=[\n",
        "            {\"time\": now_local(), \"value\": 19.8},\n",
        "            {\"time\": now_local(), \"value\": 20.1},\n",
        "        ],\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "    zone_id=zone_a.id,\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "chan3 = writer.create_channel(\n",
        "    KronicleChannel(\n",
        "        name=\"outdoor-temp\",\n",
        "        channel_schema=schema,\n",
        "        tags={\"zone\": \"outdoor\"},\n",
        "        rows=[\n",
        "            {\"time\": now_local(), \"value\": 5.3},\n",
        "            {\"time\": now_local(), \"value\": 4.8},\n",
        "        ],\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "    zone_id=zone_b.id,\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Channel 1: {chan1.name} in zone {zone_a.name} (id: {chan1.id})\")\n",
        "print(f\"Channel 2: {chan2.name} in zone {zone_a.name} (id: {chan2.id})\")\n",
        "print(f\"Channel 3: {chan3.name} in zone {zone_b.name} (id: {chan3.id})\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 5.5 Inspect default roles\n",
        "\n",
        "Kronicle seeds 7 default roles on first boot. Let's see what permissions they grant:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "roles = rbac.list_roles()\n",
        "print(\"Default roles:\")\n",
        "for r in roles:\n",
        "    print(f\"  {r.name:20s} — {r.description}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"    permissions: {r.permissions}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 5.6 Create a custom role\n",
        "\n",
        "We'll create a `limited_reader` role that can only read from a specific channel (not all channels):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from kronicle_sdk.models.rbac.kronicle_role import KronicleRole\n",
        "\n",
        "limited_reader = rbac.create_role(KronicleRole(\n",
        "    name=\"limited_reader\",\n",
        "    description=\"Can only read a specific channel\",\n",
        "    permissions=[\"channel:read\", \"row:read\"],\n",
        "))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Created role: {limited_reader.name} (id: {limited_reader.id})\")\n",
        "print(f\"Permissions: {limited_reader.permissions}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 5.7 Create access profiles\n",
        "\n",
        "Access profiles bind a **role** to a **resource** (zone or channel). They define *what* permissions apply *where*."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from kronicle_sdk.models.rbac.kronicle_access_profile import KronicleChannelAccess, KronicleZoneAccess\n",
        "\n",
        "# Zone-level: full writer access to zone A\n",
        "zone_a_writer_profile = rbac.create_zone_access_profile(KronicleZoneAccess(\n",
        "    name=\"lab-sensors-write\",\n",
        "    description=\"Write access to all channels in lab-sensors\",\n",
        "    role=\"data_writer\",\n",
        "    zone=zone_a,\n",
        "))\n",
        "\n",
        "# Zone-level: read-only access to zone B\n",
        "zone_b_reader_profile = rbac.create_zone_access_profile(KronicleZoneAccess(\n",
        "    name=\"weather-station-read\",\n",
        "    description=\"Read access to weather-station\",\n",
        "    role=\"data_reader\",\n",
        "    zone=zone_b,\n",
        "))\n",
        "\n",
        "# Channel-level: read-only access to lab-temp-1 only\n",
        "chan1_reader_profile = rbac.create_channel_access_profile(KronicleChannelAccess(\n",
        "    name=\"lab-temp-1-read\",\n",
        "    description=\"Read access to lab-temp-1 only\",\n",
        "    role=\"limited_reader\",\n",
        "    channel=chan1,\n",
        "))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Zone A writer profile: {zone_a_writer_profile.name} (id: {zone_a_writer_profile.id})\")\n",
        "print(f\"Zone B reader profile: {zone_b_reader_profile.name} (id: {zone_b_reader_profile.id})\")\n",
        "print(f\"Chan1 reader profile:  {chan1_reader_profile.name} (id: {chan1_reader_profile.id})\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 5.8 Create users"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from kronicle_sdk.models.rbac.kronicle_user import KronicleUser\n",
        "\n",
        "alice = rbac.create_user(KronicleUser(\n",
        "    name=\"alice\",\n",
        "    email=\"alice@kronicle.app\",\n",
        "    password=\"Alice_Passw0rd!\",\n",
        "))\n",
        "\n",
        "bob = rbac.create_user(KronicleUser(\n",
        "    name=\"bob\",\n",
        "    email=\"bob@kronicle.app\",\n",
        "    password=\"Bob_Passw0rd!\",\n",
        "))\n",
        "\n",
        "charlie = rbac.create_user(KronicleUser(\n",
        "    name=\"charlie\",\n",
        "    email=\"charlie@kronicle.app\",\n",
        "    password=\"Charlie_Passw0rd!\",\n",
        "))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"alice:   {alice.id}\")\n",
        "print(f\"bob:     {bob.id}\")\n",
        "print(f\"charlie: {charlie.id}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 5.9 Create groups and assign users"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from kronicle_sdk.models.rbac.kronicle_group import KronicleGroup\n",
        "\n",
        "writers_group = rbac.create_group(KronicleGroup(name=\"lab-writers\"))\n",
        "readers_group = rbac.create_group(KronicleGroup(name=\"lab-readers\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "# Alice is a writer\n",
        "rbac.add_user_to_group(user_id=alice.id, group_id=writers_group.id)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Bob and Charlie are readers\n",
        "rbac.add_user_to_group(user_id=bob.id, group_id=readers_group.id)\n",
        "rbac.add_user_to_group(user_id=charlie.id, group_id=readers_group.id)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Group '{writers_group.name}': alice\")\n",
        "print(f\"Group '{readers_group.name}': bob, charlie\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 5.10 Create policies\n",
        "\n",
        "Policies bind **subjects** (users or groups) to **access profiles**. This is where access is actually granted."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from kronicle_sdk.models.rbac.kronicle_policy import KronicleZonePolicy, KronicleChannelPolicy\n",
        "from kronicle_sdk.models.rbac.kronicle_rbac_base import KronicleRbacBase\n",
        "\n",
        "# Writers group gets write access to zone A (all channels)\n",
        "zone_write_policy = rbac.create_zone_policy(KronicleZonePolicy(\n",
        "    name=\"writers-zone-a\",\n",
        "    access_profile=zone_a_writer_profile,\n",
        "    subject=KronicleRbacBase(name=writers_group.name, id=writers_group.id),\n",
        "))\n",
        "\n",
        "# Bob gets read access to zone B (weather station)\n",
        "zone_bob_read_policy = rbac.create_zone_policy(KronicleZonePolicy(\n",
        "    name=\"bob-read-zone-b\",\n",
        "    access_profile=zone_b_reader_profile,\n",
        "    subject=KronicleRbacBase(name=bob.name, id=bob.id),\n",
        "))\n",
        "\n",
        "# Charlie gets read access to lab-temp-1 only (via the limited_reader role)\n",
        "chan_charlie_policy = rbac.create_channel_policy(KronicleChannelPolicy(\n",
        "    name=\"charlie-read-lab-temp-1\",\n",
        "    access_profile=chan1_reader_profile,\n",
        "    subject=KronicleRbacBase(name=charlie.name, id=charlie.id),\n",
        "))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Policies created:\")\n",
        "print(f\"  {zone_write_policy.name}: {writers_group.name} → {zone_a_writer_profile.name}\")\n",
        "print(f\"  {zone_bob_read_policy.name}: bob → {zone_b_reader_profile.name}\")\n",
        "print(f\"  {chan_charlie_policy.name}: charlie → {chan1_reader_profile.name}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 5.11 Verify access control\n",
        "\n",
        "Now let's login as each user and verify what they can and cannot do."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def login_as(name, password):\n",
        "    resp = api_post(\"/auth/v1/login\", {\"name\": name, \"password\": password})\n",
        "    token = resp[\"access_token\"]\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def auth_get(path):\n",
        "        url = f\"http://localhost:8000{path}\"\n",
        "        req = urllib.request.Request(url, headers={\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\"})\n",
        "        return urllib.request.urlopen(req)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def auth_post(path, body):\n",
        "        url = f\"http://localhost:8000{path}\"\n",
        "        data = json.dumps(body).encode()\n",
        "        req = urllib.request.Request(url, data=data, headers={\n",
        "            \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n",
        "            \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\"\n",
        "        })\n",
        "        return urllib.request.urlopen(req)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    return auth_get, auth_post"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print(\"=\" * 60)\n",
        "print(\"ALICE (data_writer via lab-writers group → zone A)\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 60)\n",
        "alice_get, alice_post = login_as(\"alice\", \"Alice_Passw0rd!\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Can read channels in zone A\n",
        "resp = alice_get(\"/api/v1/channels\")\n",
        "channels = json.loads(resp.read())\n",
        "print(f\"\\nCan read channels: {[c['name'] for c in (channels if isinstance(channels, list) else [channels])]}\" \n",
        "      if channels else \"No channels visible\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Can write to lab-temp-1\n",
        "try:\n",
        "    resp = alice_post(f\"/data/v1/channels/{chan1.id}/rows\", {\n",
        "        \"rows\": [{\"time\": now_local(), \"value\": 23.0}]\n",
        "    })\n",
        "    print(f\"Can write to lab-temp-1: YES\")\n",
        "except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n",
        "    print(f\"Can write to lab-temp-1: NO ({e.code})\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print(\"=\" * 60)\n",
        "print(\"BOB (data_reader via direct zone B policy)\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 60)\n",
        "bob_get, bob_post = login_as(\"bob\", \"Bob_Passw0rd!\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Can read channels in zone B\n",
        "resp = bob_get(\"/api/v1/channels\")\n",
        "channels = json.loads(resp.read())\n",
        "print(f\"\\nVisible channels: {[c['name'] for c in (channels if isinstance(channels, list) else [channels])]}\"\n",
        "      if channels else \"No channels visible\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Cannot write (only has reader role)\n",
        "try:\n",
        "    resp = bob_post(f\"/data/v1/channels/{chan3.id}/rows\", {\n",
        "        \"rows\": [{\"time\": now_local(), \"value\": 6.0}]\n",
        "    })\n",
        "    print(f\"Can write to outdoor-temp: YES (unexpected!)\")\n",
        "except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n",
        "    print(f\"Can write to outdoor-temp: NO (403 Forbidden — expected)\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print(\"=\" * 60)\n",
        "print(\"CHARLIE (limited_reader → lab-temp-1 only)\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 60)\n",
        "charlie_get, charlie_post = login_as(\"charlie\", \"Charlie_Passw0rd!\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Can read lab-temp-1\n",
        "try:\n",
        "    resp = charlie_get(f\"/api/v1/channels/{chan1.id}/rows\")\n",
        "    data = json.loads(resp.read())\n",
        "    print(f\"\\nCan read lab-temp-1: YES ({len(data.get('rows', []))} rows)\")\n",
        "except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n",
        "    print(f\"\\nCan read lab-temp-1: NO ({e.code})\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Cannot read lab-temp-2 (different channel, no policy)\n",
        "try:\n",
        "    resp = charlie_get(f\"/api/v1/channels/{chan2.id}/rows\")\n",
        "    print(f\"Can read lab-temp-2: YES (unexpected!)\")\n",
        "except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n",
        "    print(f\"Can read lab-temp-2: NO (403 Forbidden — expected)\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Cannot read outdoor-temp (different zone)\n",
        "try:\n",
        "    resp = charlie_get(f\"/api/v1/channels/{chan3.id}/rows\")\n",
        "    print(f\"Can read outdoor-temp: YES (unexpected!)\")\n",
        "except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n",
        "    print(f\"Can read outdoor-temp: NO (403 Forbidden — expected)\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Cannot write\n",
        "try:\n",
        "    resp = charlie_post(f\"/data/v1/channels/{chan1.id}/rows\", {\n",
        "        \"rows\": [{\"time\": now_local(), \"value\": 25.0}]\n",
        "    })\n",
        "    print(f\"Can write to lab-temp-1: YES (unexpected!)\")\n",
        "except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n",
        "    print(f\"Can write to lab-temp-1: NO (403 Forbidden — expected)\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 5.12 Anonymous access\n",
        "\n",
        "When `allow_anonymous=true` in the config, unauthenticated requests are treated as belonging to the `anonymous` group.\n",
        "We can grant that group read access to a specific channel."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from kronicle_sdk.models.rbac.kronicle_group import KronicleGroup\n",
        "\n",
        "# Create an access profile for anonymous read access to outdoor-temp\n",
        "anon_profile = rbac.create_channel_access_profile(KronicleChannelAccess(\n",
        "    name=\"outdoor-temp-public\",\n",
        "    description=\"Public read access to outdoor temperature\",\n",
        "    role=\"data_reader\",\n",
        "    channel=chan3,\n",
        "))\n",
        "\n",
        "# Get the anonymous group (auto-created when allow_anonymous=true)\n",
        "groups = rbac.list_groups()\n",
        "anon_group = next((g for g in groups if g.name == \"anonymous\"), None)\n",
        "\n",
        "if anon_group:\n",
        "    anon_policy = rbac.create_channel_policy(KronicleChannelPolicy(\n",
        "        name=\"anonymous-read-outdoor\",\n",
        "        access_profile=anon_profile,\n",
        "        subject=KronicleRbacBase(name=anon_group.name, id=anon_group.id),\n",
        "    ))\n",
        "    print(f\"Anonymous policy created: {anon_policy.name}\")\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(\"Anonymous group not found. Make sure allow_anonymous=true in your config.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Anonymous request — no token\n",
        "try:\n",
        "    resp = http_get(f\"/api/v1/channels/{chan3.id}/rows\")\n",
        "    data = json.loads(resp.read())\n",
        "    print(f\"Anonymous can read outdoor-temp: YES ({len(data.get('rows', []))} rows)\")\n",
        "except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n",
        "    print(f\"Anonymous read failed: {e.code}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Anonymous cannot read lab channels (no policy)\n",
        "try:\n",
        "    resp = http_get(f\"/api/v1/channels/{chan1.id}/rows\")\n",
        "    print(f\"Anonymous can read lab-temp-1: YES (unexpected!)\")\n",
        "except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n",
        "    print(f\"Anonymous read lab-temp-1: NO (403 Forbidden — expected)\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 5.13 Summary of RBAC entities\n",
        "\n",
        "| Entity | Purpose | Example |\n",
        "|--------|---------|---------|\n",
        "| **Role** | Named set of permissions | `data_reader` → `channel:read`, `row:read` |\n",
        "| **Access Profile** | Binds a role to a resource | `lab-temp-1-read` → `limited_reader` + `lab-temp-1` channel |\n",
        "| **Policy** | Binds a subject (user/group) to an access profile | `charlie-read-lab-temp-1` → charlie + `lab-temp-1-read` profile |\n",
        "| **Subject** | User or group that receives a policy | `charlie` or `lab-writers` |\n",
        "\n",
        "**Permission evaluation chain:** user roles → group roles → zone policies → channel policies → row policies.\n",
        "\n",
        "Deny always overrides allow. Resource-level policies override zone-level policies."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## 6. Testing the App (Dev)\n",
        "\n",
        "This section covers running the test suite during development."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 6.1 Unit tests\n",
        "\n",
        "Unit tests run without a server or database. They test individual modules in isolation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!pytest tests/unit/ -v --tb=short"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 6.2 Integration tests\n",
        "\n",
        "Integration tests require a running Kronicle server. They test the full request/response cycle\n",
        "through the API connectors.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Prerequisites:**\n",
        "- Kronicle server running (e.g. `podman-compose up -d`)\n",
        "- Environment variables set (from `.conf/.integration.env`):\n",
        "  - `KRONICLE_USR_NAME` / `KRONICLE_USR_PASS` — regular user credentials\n",
        "  - `KRONICLE_SU_NAME` / `KRONICLE_SU_PASS` — superuser credentials"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Integration tests (requires running server + env vars)\n",
        "# !source .conf/.integration.env && pytest tests/integration/ -v -m integration\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Run this in your terminal (not in the notebook):\")\n",
        "print(\"  source .conf/.integration.env && pytest tests/integration/ -v -m integration\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 6.3 Run all tests together"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print(\"Run this in your terminal:\")\n",
        "print(\"  source .conf/.integration.env && pytest --run-all\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 6.4 Coverage report\n",
        "\n",
        "Coverage is configured in `pyproject.toml` and runs automatically with `pytest`.\n",
        "Reports are generated in `reports/`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!pytest --cov=kronicle --cov-report=term-missing --cov-report=html:reports/html_dir"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 6.5 Test structure\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "tests/\n",
        "├── conftest.py              # --run-all flag\n",
        "├── unit/                    # No server required\n",
        "│   ├── api/\n",
        "│   ├── auth/\n",
        "│   ├── db/\n",
        "│   ├── schemas/\n",
        "│   ├── services/\n",
        "│   └── ...\n",
        "└── integration/             # Requires running server\n",
        "    ├── conftest.py          # Env var checks, auto-marks tests\n",
        "    ├── auth/\n",
        "    ├── data/\n",
        "    ├── rbac/\n",
        "    └── setup/\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Integration tests are automatically skipped unless:\n",
        "- `-m integration` is passed, or\n",
        "- `--run-all` is passed, and\n",
        "- `KRONICLE_USR_NAME`, `KRONICLE_USR_PASS`, `KRONICLE_SU_NAME`, `KRONICLE_SU_PASS` are set."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 6.6 Linting & formatting"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
